@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Jaeger implementation progress
+
+## 2026-11-18 — preserve incomplete background work
+
+Owner directive: finish the existing product in verified increments; protect the
+Mac Studio runtime. This checkpoint is development-only, not a deployed release.
+
+### Working now
+
+The existing Gateway task owner persists admission, checkpoints, retries,
+cancellation and result delivery. Reused it; no new scheduler or runtime owner.
+Reproduced a defect where an unfinished artifact caused a yielded, blocked,
+needs-owner or errored worker receipt to become `completed_verified`.
+
+The owner now considers worker errors and halt reasons before artifact verification.
+Yielded work remains queued; owner questions and blockers retain their states;
+failed work uses the existing bounded retry policy. Successful recovery clears
+the previous error. Tests reopen the SQLite store and event bus, resume the next
+attempt from its checkpoint, write the final artifact and deliver one result.
+The worker in these tests is deterministic Python, not a live model.
+
+### Changes
+
+- `jaeger_ai/core/tasks/owner.py`: correct completion precedence and stale errors.
+- `dev/tests/jaeger_ai/core/test_gateway_task_owner.py`: seven regression cases,
+  including checkpoint/retry recovery after reopening persisted state.
+- `scripts/verify.sh`: add `tasks` target and include it in backend verification.
+- Two IDE activation fixtures: disposable mocked home and subscription disposal,
+  preventing operator-state writes and test servers surviving fixture teardown.
+
+### Validation
+
+| Check | Observed result |
+| --- | --- |
+| New regressions before repair | Six failures: partial artifacts falsely completed work |
+| New regressions after repair | Seven passed (added error-retry recovery case) |
+| `./scripts/verify.sh tasks` | 52 passed |
+| Gateway durability (backend pipeline) | 14 passed |
+| Git and repository hygiene | Passed; 8 hygiene tests; disk scan found no source caches/state |
+| IDE fixture regressions | 9 passed; process exited normally |
+| IDE suite (full pipeline) | 300 passed |
+| Full pipeline | Stops at shared UI: `tsc: command not found`; isolated checkout has no frontend dependencies |
+| Backend pipeline | Stops at interaction tiers: 5 failed, 1 passed |
+| Original commit comparison | Same five tier failures reproduced at unmodified `e0060074` |
+| Live service health, read-only | Gateway/WebUI/voice HTTP 200; MCP HTTP 401 (auth enforced) |
+
+The five existing tier failures concern the tier enum, autonomy default, settings
+catalog, admission of an invalid tier while a session is busy, and proactive
+background admission semantics. These require inspection against intended
+product behavior, not simply changing tests to pass.
+
+### Eight framework responsibilities: evidence boundary
+
+| Responsibility | This session's evidence |
+| --- | --- |
+| Models | Existing routing preserved; no live inference acceptance performed |
+| Tools | Existing Gateway executor reused; no live computer-operation proof |
+| Execution loop | Bounded deterministic worker resumed persisted partial work |
+| State and memory | Real SQLite checkpoint, receipt and delivery tests passed; long-term memory not qualified |
+| Permissions | Proposal/approval and cancellation regression coverage passed; autonomy tier gate still failing |
+| Orchestration | Existing task ownership retained; no specialist deployment/acceptance performed |
+| Reliability | Recovery, cancellation and duplicate-delivery regression coverage passed |
+| Events | Persisted event bus/delivery tests passed; native UI acceptance not performed |
+
+### Runtime-boundary incident
+
+During an initial full verification rerun with loopback sockets allowed, existing
+IDE activation fixtures used the real OS home and ignored subscription disposal.
+They wrote `~/.jaeger/run/vscode-bridge.json` and left test listeners alive.
+Stopped only the identified test children (PIDs 62982 and 62992). Removed the
+descriptor only after confirming its PID matched those children. Its previous
+contents were not captured, so restoration of any prior descriptor cannot be
+claimed. No credentials were printed. The two fixtures now isolate the mocked
+home and dispose their subscriptions; subsequent IDE runs exited normally, and
+the operator descriptor remained absent. Host-model bridge discovery may need
+owner-authorized restoration if it was in use. No production service was
+restarted, rebuilt, uninstalled or deployed; production tracked source and HEAD
+remain unchanged. Existing untracked user files were left alone.
+
+### Artifacts and continuation
+
+- Base: `e00600741ed11ebb0d05480f1f51eecb4eb528d9`.
+- Isolated branch: `codex/durable-task-recovery`.
+- Working copy: `/private/tmp/jaeger-autonomy-dev-20261118`.
+- Durable review package:
+  `~/Documents/JaegerAI-Development/2026-11-18-durable-task-recovery/`.
+  Contains commit metadata, patch, incremental Git bundle, this report and logs.
+- Logs: `jaeger-autonomy-*.log`; keep failed runs as evidence alongside passing runs.
+
+First milestone remains unqualified: health endpoints do not prove a working
+chat/voice loop. Persistent background execution has a repaired, tested slice;
+this does not prove autonomous model-driven self-development or a video pipeline.
+No fabricated progress percentage; one background completion defect eliminated
+in development, plus a verification isolation defect repaired.
+
+Next task: reconcile the failing interaction-tier/background admission contract
+against the owner's intended autonomy, then verify an authorized bounded task
+through the actual isolated Gateway and model. Install development-only frontend
+dependencies before claiming the full verification gate. Production deployment
+and restarts still require separate permission under the latest directive.
